UPSTREAM SOURCES

  U.S. Department of Health and Human Services: COVID-19 Reported Patient Impact and Hospital Capacity by Facility,
  dataset anag-cw7u, healthdata.gov (final update May 2024, last week 21 April 2024).
  https://healthdata.gov/Hospital/COVID-19-Reported-Patient-Impact-and-Hospital-Capa/anag-cw7u
  A work of the United States Government, public domain in the United States (17 U.S.C. 105).
  Changes: Los Angeles County rows only, from the week of 7 June 2020; suppressed small counts (-999999) left blank;
  record 05T782 dropped (it repeats 050782 week for week from December 2022) and 05T485 (a temporary site) added to
  050485; shares in use worked out from the beds and beds in use; names in title case with acronyms restored and two
  misspellings corrected; each hospital drawn as a disc 1 km across at its geocoded address.

  U.S. Census Bureau: Cartographic Boundary Files 2022, census tracts, California (1:500,000); American Community Survey 2018-2022
  5-year estimates, table B01003 (total population), census tracts. Public domain.
  Changes: Los Angeles County tracts; the straight-line distance from a point inside each tract to the nearest general
  hospital, and beds per 1,000 people within 5, 10 and 20 km (a two-step ratio), worked out by us.

  Base map in the Plotlay project and the app screenshots
